  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **So Live** (1 review): Listener calls So Live a treat and says it made the show feel like a throwback [3]\n- **Drum Solo** (1 review): The drum solo sat in the middle of One In Seven, splitting it into two parts [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Greeting From Neal Evans**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Drum Solo**: back after 36 archived shows (1105 days); rare: 10 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2016-03-25.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 6 songs; 74 min; rated 4.5/5 by 2 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Listener lists an intro first, then Outrage, and an untitled new song placed eighth between Lenny and PJ's [2]\n- Listener says Hat Trick ran across two consecutive slots, followed by Spark and Lenny [2]\n- One In Seven was played at its original tempo, unlike other versions [3]\n- The band sounded tight, which is not always so when they play a few one-off songs [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2016-03-25.flac16**: taped by Z-Man; transferred by Z-Man; source: Schoeps CCM4V's>Lunatec V2>Benchmark AD2K> Sound Devices 722 (24/44) [1]",
